# Global gitignore, read by git at this path with no config pointing at it —
# core.excludesFile is unset, and this is the default it falls back to.
#
# For patterns that follow the machine rather than the project: files a local
# tool drops into any checkout, which every repo would otherwise have to ignore
# on its own. Anything inherent to a project belongs in that project's
# .gitignore instead, where collaborators get it too.

# Claude Code writes per-checkout permissions here. Machine-local by design,
# and never the same twice, so no shared .gitignore can be relied on to cover it.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
